  "scope": "A single-node local Kind v0.32.0 and Kubernetes v1.36.1 cluster. The API server allocates addresses in deliberately small IPv4 ServiceCIDRs. The case reads native ServiceCIDR/IPAddress allocations, reports a synthetic two-address low-spare threshold, and creates case-owned events.events.k8s.io/v1 Warning/Normal records from the test harness. A second ServiceCIDR adds capacity, and both ClusterIP Services serve the same owned marker through cluster DNS. Node PodCIDR containment is inspected. The event producer is modeled, not a deployed monitoring controller. CNI Pod IPAM sizing, node pool exhaustion, dual-stack, production telemetry, and alert routing require separate evidence.",
